1d] Scope table headers explicitly</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"> 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"push\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"leaves-a-trace\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git push</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git push\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git push\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">To github.com:localis/handbook.git</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"push-range\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">   a1b2c3d..7a3c91d  main -&gt; main</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"discard-commit\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reset --hard HEAD~1</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reset --hard HEAD~1\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reset --hard HEAD~1\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"reset-moved\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">HEAD is now at a1b2c3d Add conformance canary</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"find-in-reflog\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reflog</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reflog\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reflog\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">a1b2c3d (HEAD -&gt; main) HEAD@{0}: reset: moving to HEAD~1</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"reflog-lost-commit\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">7a3c91d (origin/main) HEAD@{1}: commit: Scope table headers explicitly</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">a1b2c3d HEAD@{2}: commit: Add conformance canary</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"recover-from-reflog\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reset --hard 7a3c91d</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reset --hard &lt;sha-from-your-reflog&gt;\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reset --hard &lt;sha-from-your-reflog&gt;\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"recover-moved\" data-focused=\"true\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">HEAD is now at 7a3c91d Scope table headers explicitly</span></div></div><div data-role=\"ready-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div></div></section></div><div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"check-status--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>git status reads the repository and reports what has changed. It never modifies anything, so it is always safe to run.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"check-status--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>HeaderFix.jsx has edits that are not staged, and NewCanary.jsx is new and untracked. Only the edit to HeaderFix.jsx belongs in this lesson's commit.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-status\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git status documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The -p (patch) option presents the file's changes one hunk at a time, so you decide exactly what goes into the next commit.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>This hunk replaces the hard-coded scope with a prop that falls back to the old value.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s03\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Git now waits for a decision about this hunk.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s04\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Answering y adds this hunk to the index. The file on disk is unchanged, and nothing is committed yet.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-add\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git add documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"review-staged--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>--cached compares the index with the last commit, so this is exactly what the next commit will contain.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"review-staged--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>One file, one line replaced. NewCanary.jsx is not included, because it was never staged.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-diff\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git diff documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"commit--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The staged change becomes a permanent snapshot with a message describing why it was made.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"commit--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Commit 7a3c91d now exists on main, but only on this machine until it is pushed.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-commit\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git commit documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"push--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>push sends your new commits to origin so other people can pull them.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"push--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>origin/main moved from a1b2c3d to 7a3c91d. Others can now fetch this commit.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-push\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git push documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"discard-commit--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Before copying: run git status and stash or commit any work you want to keep. reset --hard moves main back one commit and overwrites both the index and the working tree to match it.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"discard-commit--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Local main is back at a1b2c3d. Commit 7a3c91d is no longer on main, though origin/main still points to it because it was pushed. Any uncommitted work would have been lost for good.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reset\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reset documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"find-in-reflog--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The reflog records every place HEAD has pointed on this machine, including commits no local branch reaches anymore.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"find-in-reflog--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>7a3c91d is one step back in the reflog, so its SHA is available to recover it.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reflog\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reflog documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"recover-from-reflog--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Before copying: confirm the target in your own reflog and preserve uncommitted work. In this lesson, reset --hard is the recovery step: it returns main to 7a3c91d, the commit found in the reflog.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"recover-from-reflog--s02\" aria-current=\"step\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The commit is back and main matches origin/main again. Using the command to rescue work does not make it safe: it still overwrites the index and working tree, so uncommitted changes would be lost.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reset\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reset documentation</a><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reflog\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-02\">Git reflog documentation</a></div></div>",
        "after": "<div><section data-cim-renderer=\"console/v1\" data-step=\"recover-from-reflog--s02\"><header data-role=\"titlebar\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\"><span data-role=\"title\">git — localis/handbook</span><span data-role=\"risk-badge\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\">CANNOT BE UNDONE</span></header><div data-role=\"transcript\"><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"check-status\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git status</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git status\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git status\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">On branch main</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"status-up-to-date\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">Your branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"></span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">Changes not staged for commit:</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">  (use \"git add &lt;file&gt;...\" to update what will be committed)</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">  (use \"git restore &lt;file&gt;...\" to discard changes in working directory)</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"warning\" data-output-id=\"status-modified\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">        modified:   src/HeaderFix.jsx</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"></span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">Untracked files:</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">  (use \"git add &lt;file&gt;...\" to include in what will be committed)</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"warning\" data-output-id=\"status-untracked\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">        src/NewCanary.jsx</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"></span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">no changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"stage-hunk\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"free-to-undo\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git add -p -- src/HeaderFix.jsx</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git add -p -- src/HeaderFix.jsx\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git add -p -- src/HeaderFix.jsx\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">diff --git a/src/HeaderFix.jsx b/src/HeaderFix.jsx</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">index 3f2c1a9..8d04e7b 100644</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">--- a/src/HeaderFix.jsx</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">+++ b/src/HeaderFix.jsx</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">@@ -15,3 +15,3 @@ export function HeaderFix(props) {</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">   const rows = props.rows;</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"removed\" data-output-id=\"hunk-removed\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">-  const scope = 'col';</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"added\" data-output-id=\"hunk-added\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">+  const scope = props.scope ?? 'col';</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">   return (</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"hunk-prompt\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">(1/1) Stage this hunk [y,n,q,a,d,e,?]?</span><span data-role=\"response-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"response\">y</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"review-staged\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git diff --cached --stat</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git diff --cached --stat\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git diff --cached --stat\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"stat-file\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"> src/HeaderFix.jsx | 2 +-</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"> 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"commit\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"leaves-a-trace\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git commit -m \"Scope table headers explicitly\"</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git commit -m &quot;Scope table headers explicitly&quot;\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git commit -m &quot;Scope table headers explicitly&quot;\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"commit-created\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">[main 7a3c91d] Scope table headers explicitly</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\"> 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"push\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"leaves-a-trace\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git push</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git push\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git push\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"dim\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">To github.com:localis/handbook.git</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"push-range\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">   a1b2c3d..7a3c91d  main -&gt; main</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"discard-commit\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reset --hard HEAD~1</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reset --hard HEAD~1\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reset --hard HEAD~1\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"reset-moved\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">HEAD is now at a1b2c3d Add conformance canary</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"find-in-reflog\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reflog</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reflog\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reflog\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">a1b2c3d (HEAD -&gt; main) HEAD@{0}: reset: moving to HEAD~1</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"reflog-lost-commit\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">7a3c91d (origin/main) HEAD@{1}: commit: Scope table headers explicitly</span></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">a1b2c3d HEAD@{2}: commit: Add conformance canary</span></div></div><div data-role=\"entry\" data-beat=\"recover-from-reflog\"><div data-role=\"command-line\"><span data-role=\"risk-mark\" data-risk=\"cannot-be-undone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"command\">git reset --hard 7a3c91d</span><button type=\"button\" data-role=\"copy\" data-copy=\"git reset --hard &lt;sha-from-your-reflog&gt;\" aria-label=\"Copy command: git reset --hard &lt;sha-from-your-reflog&gt;\">Copy</button></div><div data-role=\"output-line\" data-tone=\"normal\" data-output-id=\"recover-moved\" data-focused=\"true\"><span data-role=\"output-text\">HEAD is now at 7a3c91d Scope table headers explicitly</span></div></div><div data-role=\"ready-line\"><span data-role=\"prompt\">~/localis/handbook (main) $</span><span data-role=\"prompt-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </span><span data-role=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div></div></section></div><div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"check-status--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>git status reads the repository and reports what has changed. It never modifies anything, so it is always safe to run.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"check-status--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>HeaderFix.jsx has edits that are not staged, and NewCanary.jsx is new and untracked. Only the edit to HeaderFix.jsx belongs in this lesson's commit.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-status\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git status documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The -p (patch) option presents the file's changes one hunk at a time, so you decide exactly what goes into the next commit.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>This hunk replaces the hard-coded scope with a prop that falls back to the old value.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s03\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Git now waits for a decision about this hunk.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"stage-hunk--s04\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Answering y adds this hunk to the index. The file on disk is unchanged, and nothing is committed yet.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-add\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git add documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"review-staged--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>--cached compares the index with the last commit, so this is exactly what the next commit will contain.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"review-staged--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>One file, one line replaced. NewCanary.jsx is not included, because it was never staged.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-diff\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git diff documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"commit--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The staged change becomes a permanent snapshot with a message describing why it was made.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"commit--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Commit 7a3c91d now exists on main, but only on this machine until it is pushed.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-commit\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git commit documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"push--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>push sends your new commits to origin so other people can pull them.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"push--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>origin/main moved from a1b2c3d to 7a3c91d. Others can now fetch this commit.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-push\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git push documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"discard-commit--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Before copying: run git status and stash or commit any work you want to keep. reset --hard moves main back one commit and overwrites both the index and the working tree to match it.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"discard-commit--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Local main is back at a1b2c3d. Commit 7a3c91d is no longer on main, though origin/main still points to it because it was pushed. Any uncommitted work would have been lost for good.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reset\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reset documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"find-in-reflog--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The reflog records every place HEAD has pointed on this machine, including commits no local branch reaches anymore.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"find-in-reflog--s02\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>7a3c91d is one step back in the reflog, so its SHA is available to recover it.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reflog\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reflog documentation</a></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"recover-from-reflog--s01\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>Before copying: confirm the target in your own reflog and preserve uncommitted work. In this lesson, reset --hard is the recovery step: it returns main to 7a3c91d, the commit found in the reflog.</p></div><div data-cim-selected=\"false\" data-cim-step-id=\"recover-from-reflog--s02\" aria-current=\"step\"><button type=\"button\"></button><p>The commit is back and main matches origin/main again. Using the command to rescue work does not make it safe: it still overwrites the index and working tree, so uncommitted changes would be lost.</p><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reset\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-01\">Git reset documentation</a><a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reflog\" data-cim-link-id=\"ref-02\">Git reflog documentation</a></div></div>"
      }
    ]
